    "pdpPlainTextPreview": "A special 2023-dated Sovereign celebrating the historic coronation of His Majesty The King\nWE ARE STRENGTHENING ACCOUNT SECURITY AND PROTECTING YOUR ACCESS WITH 2 STEP VERIFICATION. FIND OUT MORE Home Sovereign All Sovereign Coins 2023 Charles III Gold Proof Coronation Sovereign Share via Gold Proof 2023 Charles III Gold Proof Coronation Sovereign Price: £1,285.00 EMAIL ME WHEN IN STOCK Email Me When In Stock PRODUCT CODE: HISC2023PS Struck in 2023 to mark the coronation year of His Majesty King Charles III Features an exclusive crowned effigy of King Charles III, created especially for the coronation issue Obverse shows His Majesty wearing a crown, a rare departure from the usual uncrowned profile Reverse carries Benedetto Pistrucci’s classic St George and the dragon, maintaining the long sovereign tradition First coronation‑year sovereign of the new Carolean era, a key early date for modern series collectors Proof finish with frosted portrait and devices contrasted against mirrored fields Distinctive combination of crowned obverse and traditional reverse, unique within Charles III sovereign issues to date Gold Proof Read the full description YOU MIGHT ALSO BE INTERESTED IN ADD TO BASKET Britannia 2026 1oz Silver Bullion Coin £62.52 In Stock ADD TO BASKET Britannia 2022 1 oz Silver Bullion Coin £61.32 In Stock ADD TO BASKET Level 5 Genius Medal £9.95 In Stock ADD TO BASKET Britannia 2026 1oz Gold Bullion Coin £3,487.00 In Stock ADD TO BASKET 100th Anniversary of the Birth of Queen Elizabeth II 2026 UK £5 Brilliant Uncirculated Coin £17.50 In Stock ADD TO BASKET Britannia 2026 1oz Silver Bullion Twenty-Five Coin Tube £1,483.00 In Stock ADD TO BASKET Level 4 Mastermind Medal £9.95 In Stock ADD TO BASKET Britannia 1g Gold Bullion Minted Bar £140.78 In Stock ADD TO BASKET Level 3 Decoder Medal £9.95 In Stock ADD TO BASKET Level 2 Explorer Medal and Collector Folder £9.95 In Stock Struck to mark the coronation year of His Majesty King Charles III, the 2023 Gold Proof Coronation Sovereign unites a specially created crowned effigy with the classic St George and the dragon reverse. It stands at the beginning of the new Carolean chapter for the sovereign, echoing earlier coronation‑year issues while remaining firmly rooted in the modern era. The obverse features an exclusive crowned portrait of King Charles III, created for the coronation and used only on a select group of coins. The monarch is shown facing left, wearing the Tudor crown, with the Latin legend naming him as king running around the rim. Finished to proof standard, the portrait is presented in frosted relief against mirror‑polished fields, drawing out the finely engraved detail of crown, hair and drapery in a way that rewards close examination under magnification. On the reverse, Benedetto Pistrucci’s iconic St George and the dragon returns in its traditional form, a conscious link to more than two centuries of sovereign history. The dynamic composition of horse, rider and dragon is rendered in crisp relief, the 2023 date in the exergue quietly signalling the coronation year. The combination of a coronation‑only crowned effigy with the familiar reverse creates a sovereign that is both immediately recognisable and clearly distinguished within any run of modern issues. For the collector, the 2023 Charles III Gold Proof Coronation Sovereign offers several compelling attractions: it is the first coronation‑year sovereign of the Carolean era, the inaugural proof sovereign pairing a crowned effigy of the new monarch with the classic St George design, and a key early date in the developing Charles III series. Struck to the highest proof standard with a milled edge and crisply defined denticles, it forms a dignified and historically resonant addition to any cabinet devoted to the sovereign and the great ceremonial milestones of the British monarchy. SPECIFICATION Specification Value Denomination Sovereign Alloy 22 Carat Gold Weight 7.980g Diameter 22.05mm Reverse Designer Benede"
